{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D(382|384|489|490|491|505|66[5-9]|67[0-5])\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS.md; rg -n '\"'^#{1,5} '\"' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md clean-arch/PRD.md\"","aggregated_output":"553:| D209 | 2026-10-28 | A statement no open question takes is dropped at extraction; evaluation reads the dropped record, not a sid… | in force (amended by D264; for the clean path by D382, D383) | §6 Extraction |\n726:| D382 | 2026-11-08 | Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason | in force | clean-arch PRD §12 |\n728:| D384 | 2026-11-08 | Clean Step 1 opens only the big matters, by the signed standard as the frozen gold applies it | in force | clean-arch PRD §12 |\n775:| D431 | 2026-11-12 | D427's end-to-end comparison is against production as it now runs (no preset questions, D370), frozen ruler, same day (for a run longer than a day, D667), three draws each; the seven graded questions beside; the seeded comparison stays a diagnostic | in force | `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/kr-consensus.md` |\n793:| D449 | 2026-11-13 | Wiring code review: shared stops read before every send, launcher liveness by its registered lock, the agreed reservation bound, the real orchestration proved; redo of Step 1, Step 2, production only by a reasoned relaunch; a crash stops the run (council consensus, D439; across draws, replaced for the release comparison by one ledger per draw, D667) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/run_fresh.py` |\n833:| D489 | 2026-11-14 | The fresh week (one draw a system): not clear by the rule written before reading, no system chosen; production covers 4 of 5 big matters and the clean path 2 (it lacks revenue and margin, D382/D384); whether the new system holds questions on the company's main numbers goes to Alex with three options (council consensus) | in force; Alex chose the test (D490) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md` |\n834:| D490 | 2026-11-14 | Alex opens a test arm of clean Step 1 that may open questions on the company's revenue and margin (\"试开这类问题\"): a probe of a few cents on the stored week first, the second fresh week only if it meets its lines; D382 and D384 stay in force for the adopted path | in force; the test ran and its arm was stopped (D491) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` §4 |\n835:| D491 | 2026-11-14 | The revenue-and-margin test arm (c20) opens the three questions with no number cards but fails its probe on a line written beforehand (the Vera Rubin question not opened, 0 of 3 against 2 of 3; cause not settled); stopped, not adopted; the next step goes to Alex (council consensus) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/RESULT.md` |\n837:| D493 | 2026-11-14 | Reflection council (D492): every change from D439 to D491 was words in the one Step 1 call and moved a neighbour; the reader's loss is around the company's main numbers; no further request change now; next a $0 test of the kept figures assembled as a company record; the standing-question comparison stays a candidate that goes to Alex first (D370) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/record/RECORD-TEST-DESIGN.md` |\n846:| D502 | 2026-11-15 | The table test: no wrong join found in the ten joined lines, all four table readers meet the written answer line, no reliable saving of effort shown; the table goes to Alex as a tested mock, not as the accepted handling of revenue and margin; D489's comparison unchanged; the next step is his (council consensus) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/record-3/TABLE-TEST-RESULT.md` |\n847:| D503 | 2026-11-15 | Alex reviews the mock table and opens a $0 reading on the fresh week of D489: the same table from that week's stored answers, read blind for the three matters the new system had no question for; a separate question, D489's count unchanged | in force; the test ran (D504) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` §10 |\n848:| D504 | 2026-11-15 | The table on the fresh week: M01 undecided, M02 and M03 not findable by the line; eleven of twelve key figures are in the table, two of four readers found all eleven; the table passes on stored-label faults; D489 unchanged (\"not clear\"), nothing ranks the systems; one product question goes to Alex: see the figures, a tracked question with a judgement, kept figures reaching related judgements, or several (council consensus) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/record-3/TABLE-WEEK-RESULT.md` |\n849:| D505 | 2026-11-15 | Alex: the kept financial figures should reach the judgements of related questions (not a table, not questions of their own; D382 and D384 stand); first a $0 check on the stored fresh-week run: is a kept financial figure a judgement should have received absent from its request | in force; the check ran (D506) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` §11 |\n856:| D512 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (reflection council \"my\"): neither system has earned the choice and D489 stays \"not clear\"; the next step is a decision page for Alex on which system carries forward, prepared and reviewed while he is away; no further reading or send before it; production stays the default (council consensus) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-15.md` |\n892:| D548 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (council consensus): the gates the new system must pass, listed from the record (Stage A on Alex's lines; Stage B; the end-to-end comparison; use on unseen news as proposed lines; integration); the first blocker is the worthwhile questions its answer-choice step declines, framed at $0 | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/NEW-SYSTEM-FRAME.md` (gate order superseded by D665) |\n908:| D564 | 2026-11-16 | The fortnight read (council consensus): no held question re-opened; gate 1 still not met in the product condition (7 or 5 of 13 right); no last answer unsupported by both readers, 6 of 12 contested; the page fix (processing steps and completed days at the writer) accepted for completed replays; the due-date class is one matter; next a $0 sizing of D505's company-figure delivery gap, facts linked elsewhere included | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md` |\n953:| D609 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (reflection council, cold Codex read): the next production step is a $0 source-to-request trace of the company's own figures on the carried fortnight (D505), by member, with time, duplicate, population and relevance controls and an independent second reader on bearing cases; moves only on a shared, consequential delivery mechanism | in force | `reflection-5/codex-cold.md`, `reflection-5/codex-challenge-1.md` |\n954:| D610 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (reflection council): the company-figure delivery route closes narrowly (5 bearing undelivered statements on 3 questions, two mechanisms, none predicted to move an answer by a blind second reader with working controls; 49 groups homeless by D382/D384); no v12 effect test; next a $0 feasibility review of a same-news product comparison from established libraries | in force | `delivery-trace/RESULT.md` |\n1009:| D665 | 2026-11-17 | Council (Alex: \"run your council to determine\"): the six lines stop blocking release (reported; code-decidable parts stay hard); one product comparison against poc-v118 decides readiness: big matters served, practical lead/loss/no winner written before the first send, guardrails, sizes; D431 frozen reading printed beside; Step 2 checks kept; gate 5 waits; back to Alex on any verdict | in force | D665 record; clean-arch/PRD.md §1.5 |\n1010:| D666 | 2026-11-17 | Alex: \"write a run plan and monitor it carefully and don't scope drift\": run D665's comparison once its plan passes council review; $250 runaway guard, not a budget (single ledger superseded for this run by D667); out-of-scope findings recorded only | in force | D666 record; docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md |\n1011:| D667 | 2026-11-17 | Council (run-plan rounds 1–10): the release comparison's run plan v9; full exposure census by plan §1.2 (production-replay and raw-corpus-copy exemptions only); company figures in N, subgroup printed; one ledger per draw ($65 / $25, $270); D431's same day for a run over one day (six draws launched within an hour, sends within 72 h); no replacement counts; scoring rules plan §1.4; Step 2 lines hard; two floors not measured | in force | D667 record; docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v9.md |\n1012:| D668 | 2026-11-17 | Under D667: every old replay reaching the span is a read (folder level, two blind readers); scored window 08-31..09-20 (narrowed by D669); warm-up 07-01..08-30 unfiltered; census reads every kept article in the window | in force | docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/replay-folders.json |\n1013:| D669 | 2026-11-17 | Alex: \"只排除真被读过的，比9/7–9/20\": scored window 09-07..09-20; not reads = corpus storage, pool lists, code-only corpus censuses; everything else is a read (rule frozen in stage0/classify_reads.py after council check) | in force | D669 record |\n1014:| D670 | 2026-11-17 | Under D669 (council check): 410 of 502 articles of 09-07..09-20 kept and frozen (stage0/kept-articles.json); 4 reader-shown articles added as reads; 37 bulk-viewer-only articles stay excluded (split, safer course), disclosed | in force | D670 record |\n1015:| D671 | 2026-11-17 | Under D667/D668 (council): blind matter list frozen at N = 32 (7 company figures), stage0/census/matters.json; merges need both families' grouping or both blind adjudicators; two split pairs kept apart and disclosed | in force | D671 record |\n1016:| D672 | 2026-11-17 | Alex: \"开始跑\"; freeze-review fixes applied (per-pass check, verdict rule completed, card spec frozen, launcher git-clean/ledger/redo); scorer, card builder and §1.6 tools built during the run before any output is read (Codex refused, Claude reviewer accepted with conditions); the slice stands in for the dry run with id-order and day-state checks | in force | D672 record |\n1017:| D673 | 2026-11-17 | Under D672: the card blinding rule covers the form (fields, labels, notes, ids), not the systems' own wording; repeated form check by a closed reader; wording differences disclosed | in force | D673 record; stage0/card-spec.md |\n1018:| D674 | 2026-11-17 | Alex's goal: run and keep tackling until the comparison's criteria pass; council loop on the traces after each round that does not pass; no questions to Alex; no scope drift; frozen ruler and instruments never moved; every try logged in TRIES.md | in force | D674 record |\n1019:| D675 | 2026-11-18 | Under D672: the reading tools' council review found them not ready; fixed (six draws required, exact 10-point bar, redo store, neutral ids, debate rounds, card parsing); open readings of the frozen rule written down (guardrail shares exclude covering cards; mapping without the news) | in force | D675 record; stage0/ |\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:1:# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:12:## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:25:## 1. Goal (end to end)\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:31:## 2. The core blocker (proven)\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:57:## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:70:## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:93:## 5. What to do\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:120:## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:168:## 7. Process (no drift)\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:179:## 8. Steps and where we are\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:193:## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1:# Hivemind architecture: a market world model built the way a hedge-fund analyst works\nclean-arch/PRD.md:14:## 1. Vision, problems and what is done differently\nclean-arch/PRD.md:16:### 1.1 The vision: a market world model\nclean-arch/PRD.md:55:### 1.2 The problems it answers\nclean-arch/PRD.md:79:### 1.3 Why the running pipeline was rebuilt\nclean-arch/PRD.md:102:### 1.4 What the new system does differently\nclean-arch/PRD.md:126:### 1.5 What decides that it replaces the running pipeline (D665, superseding D548's gate order)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:171:## 2. Architecture at a glance\nclean-arch/PRD.md:222:## 3. The information the system works with\nclean-arch/PRD.md:239:## 4. Step 1: read the item\nclean-arch/PRD.md:241:### Input\nclean-arch/PRD.md:248:### What the model decides\nclean-arch/PRD.md:273:### Output\nclean-arch/PRD.md:282:### Example\nclean-arch/PRD.md:294:## 5. Step 2: find and compare related evidence\nclean-arch/PRD.md:296:### Why this is separate\nclean-arch/PRD.md:300:### Find candidate evidence\nclean-arch/PRD.md:308:### Compare with Jev\nclean-arch/PRD.md:349:## 6. Step 3: save evidence and links\nclean-arch/PRD.md:363:## 7. Step 4: judge the thesis\nclean-arch/PRD.md:370:### Two parts\nclean-arch/PRD.md:379:### What the ladder step decides\nclean-arch/PRD.md:396:### Where it stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:409:## 8. How the system is measured, and where it stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:411:### The measuring stick\nclean-arch/PRD.md:423:### Where each step stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:434:### What the measurements say\nclean-arch/PRD.md:450:## 9. Walk one item through the system\nclean-arch/PRD.md:472:## 10. Open questions\nclean-arch/PRD.md:495:## 11. Design boundary\nclean-arch/PRD.md:503:## 12. Step 1 prompt: c8, adopted (D387)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:533:### What the model receives\nclean-arch/PRD.md:539:### System prompt\nclean-arch/PRD.md:717:### Closing check\nclean-arch/PRD.md:740:### Proposed per-item input\nclean-arch/PRD.md:767:### Structured-output schema\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1058:### Illustrative output for the sample input (earlier Luna draft, kept as history)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1127:### Mapping to the Step 1 diagram\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1139:### Request review and remaining limits\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1147:## 13. Step 2 prompt: Jev request (frozen)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1151:### What Jev receives\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1159:### The question\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1172:### How the answers become the outcome\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1179:### The later link when a thesis opens\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1191:## 14. Existing components to reference during the rebuild\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1195:### Thesis and evidence database\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1203:### Source pool and golden validation data\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1214:### Source data standing in for Hummingbird\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1222:### Existing extraction reference split\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1235:### Diagram-to-code map\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1250:## 15. Future design: entity relationships and cross-entity linkage\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1254:### Why this is needed\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1258:### Separate, asynchronous relationship maintenance\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1268:### Illustration: a supplier disruption\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1272:### Questions to resolve before cross-entity production use\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1284:## 16. Earlier record\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
