{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/{RUN-PLAN.md,DESIGN-1.6.md,RUN-LOG.md} docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n 'D(382|384|489|490|491|505) \\\\|' docs/DECISIONS.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json\"","aggregated_output":"     346 docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md\n     175 docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md\n     157 docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md\n     201 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\n     879 total\n726:| D382 | 2026-11-08 | Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason | in force | clean-arch PRD §12 |\n728:| D384 | 2026-11-08 | Clean Step 1 opens only the big matters, by the signed standard as the frozen gold applies it | in force | clean-arch PRD §12 |\n833:| D489 | 2026-11-14 | The fresh week (one draw a system): not clear by the rule written before reading, no system chosen; production covers 4 of 5 big matters and the clean path 2 (it lacks revenue and margin, D382/D384); whether the new system holds questions on the company's main numbers goes to Alex with three options (council consensus) | in force; Alex chose the test (D490) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md` |\n834:| D490 | 2026-11-14 | Alex opens a test arm of clean Step 1 that may open questions on the company's revenue and margin (\"试开这类问题\"): a probe of a few cents on the stored week first, the second fresh week only if it meets its lines; D382 and D384 stay in force for the adopted path | in force; the test ran and its arm was stopped (D491) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` §4 |\n835:| D491 | 2026-11-14 | The revenue-and-margin test arm (c20) opens the three questions with no number cards but fails its probe on a line written beforehand (the Vera Rubin question not opened, 0 of 3 against 2 of 3; cause not settled); stopped, not adopted; the next step goes to Alex (council consensus) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/RESULT.md` |\n849:| D505 | 2026-11-15 | Alex: the kept financial figures should reach the judgements of related questions (not a table, not questions of their own; D382 and D384 stand); first a $0 check on the stored fresh-week run: is a kept financial figure a judgement should have received absent from its request | in force; the check ran (D506) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` §11 |\n     1\t{\n     2\t \"source\": \"clean-arch/PRD.md §1.5 (D665); RUN-PLAN-v11.md §1.4 (D667-D671)\",\n     3\t \"scored_window\": [\n     4\t  \"2026-09-07\",\n     5\t  \"2026-09-20\"\n     6\t ],\n     7\t \"cutoff\": \"2026-09-20 (end of day); libraries read as they stand then; closed questions still count; timeliness not scored (days from first source to opening printed beside)\",\n     8\t \"matter_list\": \"stage0/census/matters.json\",\n     9\t \"N_frozen\": 32,\n    10\t \"covers\": \"both families mark the question opened, or narrower with both saying it carries the main outcome; broader and missed do not cover; mapping blind (each draw library under a random X/Y label, key outside the repository); a disagreement goes to two third readers, one per family; a remaining split is resolved per counting (covers > does not cover)\",\n    11\t \"same_question\": {\n    12\t  \"question\": \"an id in a system-draw library at the cutoff\",\n    13\t  \"duplicate\": \"later-opened question of a same-bet pair (A1 rule, D248)\",\n    14\t  \"distinct_bets\": \"ids less duplicates both families mark; a split duplicate counted both ways\"\n    15\t },\n    16\t \"marks\": {\n    17\t  \"worth\": [\n    18\t   \"worth\",\n    19\t   \"trivia\",\n    20\t   \"duplicate\"\n    21\t  ],\n    22\t  \"answer\": [\n    23\t   \"supported\",\n    24\t   \"unsupported\",\n    25\t   \"insufficient\",\n    26\t   \"no answer\"\n    27\t  ],\n    28\t  \"split\": \"cannot tell after the debate rounds\"\n    29\t },\n    30\t \"served_in_draw\": \"at least one covering question marked worth and supported, in each counting after split resolution\",\n    31\t \"served_by_system\": \"served in at least 2 of 3 draws\",\n    32\t \"quantities\": {\n    33\t  \"a\": \"served only by the new system\",\n    34\t  \"b\": \"served only by the old system\",\n    35\t  \"N\": \"all listed matters\"\n    36\t },\n    37\t \"countings\": {\n    38\t  \"1\": \"every split resolved to the most favourable mark its readers gave for the new system and the least favourable for the old\",\n    39\t  \"2\": \"the reverse\",\n    40\t  \"order\": {\n    41\t   \"mapping\": \"covers > does not cover\",\n    42\t   \"answer\": \"supported > insufficient > unsupported\",\n    43\t   \"worth\": \"worth > duplicate or trivia\"\n    44\t  },\n    45\t  \"resolved_insufficient\": \"outside the decided denominators\"\n    46\t },\n    47\t \"guardrails\": {\n    48\t  \"sample\": \"per system-draw: the question ids its library holds at the cutoff, sorted as strings; random.Random(20261117).sample(ids, 35), or all ids when fewer than 35; covering cards are not in the shares; the three draws pooled per system\",\n    49\t  \"shares\": [\n    50\t   \"decided figure answers unsupported\",\n    51\t   \"decided yes/no answers unsupported\",\n    52\t   \"decided worth marks trivia or duplicate\"\n    53\t  ],\n    54\t  \"beside\": [\n    55\t   \"insufficient\",\n    56\t   \"no answer\",\n    57\t   \"splits and their resolution\"\n    58\t  ],\n    59\t  \"not_exercised\": \"cannot breach; blocks only a practical lead\",\n    60\t  \"bar\": \"for each share, the new system's share minus the old system's share must be at most 10 percentage points (a larger difference is a breach)\",\n    61\t  \"exercised\": \"a subgroup is exercised only when each system has at least 10 cards in it decided without a split (pooled over its three draws)\"\n    62\t },\n    63\t \"controls\": {\n    64\t  \"planted_wrong\": \"6 in all, 3 per system: a real card of that system with its latest answer moved one rung; each needs an explicit unsupported or insufficient mark, else the reading is invalid\",\n    65\t  \"supported_controls\": \"4, each confirmed supported first by a separate closed reader before it enters the deck; at least 3 of 4 must be marked supported\",\n    66\t  \"repeats\": \"3 hidden repeats of real cards; at least 2 of 3 must receive the same marks\",\n    67\t  \"outside_product_counts\": true\n    68\t },\n    69\t \"complete_draws\": \"no release verdict without six complete draws within the D667 timing; a replacement draw is a diagnostic only\",\n    70\t \"verdict_order\": [\n    71\t  \"invalid: a plant without explicit rejection, fewer than 3 of 4 supported controls accepted, or fewer than 2 of 3 repeats marked the same\",\n    72\t  \"too small: N < 20, or fewer than 30 distinct bets in any system-draw (both ways for split duplicates)\",\n    73\t  \"practical lead: a - b >= max(3, ceil(0.15 N)) and a >= 2b under both countings, every guardrail exercised and passing under both\",\n    74\t  \"practical loss: b - a >= max(3, ceil(0.15 N)) and b >= 2a under both countings (no guardrail needed), or a breach in an exercised guardrail under both\",\n    75\t  \"no practical winner: everything else\"\n    76\t ],\n    77\t \"hard_checks\": [\n    78\t  \"D400 accounting code parts on all three passes (figure ranges end to end; favourable end stable; due day agreeing across all three sends for >= 90% of eligible questions)\",\n    79\t  \"Step 2 three lines (>= 90% recall on 100 records; <= 2% clearly wrong merges on 200; no fewer later details on 30 groups); a line short of its sample is not measured and cannot clear release\"\n    80\t ],\n    81\t \"printed_beside\": [\n    82\t  \"D428 limits\",\n    83\t  \"sign test and interval (illustrative)\",\n    84\t  \"company-figure subgroup a, b, N\",\n    85\t  \"days from first source to opening\",\n    86\t  \"D400 reader lines\",\n    87\t  \"D431 frozen-reference reading for both systems\",\n    88\t  \"floors: coverage >= 80%, trivia <= 20%, supported >= 90% from the cards; citations and omissions not measured\",\n    89\t  \"37 bulk-viewer articles excluded (kept would be 447)\",\n    90\t  \"2 split matter pairs kept apart\"\n    91\t ],\n    92\t \"card\": \"stage0/card-spec.md (frozen with this rule)\"\n    93\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
