{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|company.figure|2[5-9]/32|coverage|dry run|source'\"' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:13:## 0. Inputs, release status and the report\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:29:    line \"not measured\" below 3 company-figure theses or 20 laddered theses.\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:38:| Days from first source to opening | `score_comparison.beside` | For each matter and draw with a confirmed covering question (split covers not counted): the earliest publication day among the matter's `articles` (the census numbering), to the earliest opening day of a covering question. A question opened before 09-07 is printed \"opened in the warm-up\"; one opened in the window before that day, \"opened before the first listed article\" |\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:45:## 1. D400, all three passes\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:61:## 2. Step 2's three lines on draw new-1 (hard)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:123:## 3. D431's frozen-reference reading at 07-14 (printed beside; both systems)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:143:## 4. The floors (printed beside; proposed, not gates)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:145:As their source states them (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-10/codex-1.md`; `RUN-PLAN-v2.md` §1.6). Each floor is\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:155:## Tables\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:3:**Amendments in force over the text below:** the scored window is 2026-09-07 to 09-20 with the warm-up 07-01 to 09-06 unfiltered (D669); 410 kept articles (D670); N = 32 (D671); the scorer, the card builder and the §1.6 tools are built during the run against `stage0/verdict-rule.json` and `stage0/card-spec.md`, and reviewed before any output is read (D672); the slice stands in for the dry run (D672). Where §1.2 and §1.3 still say 07-20 or 08-31, D669 governs.\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:18:  files and the dry runs. That review, by Codex and a fresh Claude reader, gates the first paid send.\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:20:## 0. Scope\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:37:## 1. Stage 0 ($0): built, proved, frozen, then reviewed\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:39:### 1.1 Versions manifest\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:48:### 1.2 Exposure census, exclusions, one input\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:63:     - `corpus-builds.json`, frozen before any hit is read, lists the documented corpus builds: the current source, `items-window.sqlite`,\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:95:   - **Code change A:** `run_fresh.py --items` hands it to both children (clean `--source`; production `--testdb`).\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:102:### 1.3 Blind matter census (articles only; frozen before any send)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:113:4. **The company-figure flag.** Each family marks every listed matter `company figure` or not, using D505's own list: 营收、毛利率的指引、市场预期、实际业绩.\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:118:6. **De-duplication and freeze (D671).** Both families group the entries that are one bet (D248); a pair only one family grouped, or one a reviewer names, goes to one blind adjudicator of each family with its articles; a merge needs both families or both adjudicators. **Frozen:** `stage0/census/matters.json`, the only scoring list: each matter with one canonical question, its source articles, its first source day and its flag; its hash is in the versions manifest.\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:121:### 1.4 The verdict rule (`verdict-rule.json`, hashed; `score_comparison.py` with a test and a mutant per rule)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:125:   - Timeliness is not scored. The days from first source to opening are printed beside.\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:195:    - the company-figure subgroup;\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:198:### 1.5 The new system as run: code changes C to F, each with a test and a mutant\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:219:### 1.6 What D665 prints beside, with its tool and input\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:226:| Proposed absolute floors | Printed beside | Coverage ≥ 80%, trivia ≤ 20% and supported ≥ 90% come from this comparison's cards. Wrong citations ≤ 5% and zero answer-changing omissions need source-first readings this plan does not run: printed as **not measured** (agreed in the council before the send) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:228:### 1.7 Long-run risk, checked at $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:237:### 1.8 Preflight\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:245:## 2. Stage 1: the slice\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:255:## 3. Stage 2: the full run\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:273:## 4. Stage 3: reading and verdict\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:284:   - the company-figure subgroup;\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:292:## 5. Estimates (measured rates; checked at the slice)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:309:## 6. Monitoring\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:338:## 7. Returns to Alex\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '1,69p'; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '428,450p'; nl -ba poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/diagnostic-count.json; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/{old-1,new-1}\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '1,69p'; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '428,450p'; nl -ba poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/diagnostic-count.json; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/{old-1,new-1}\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n     2\t\n     3\t> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n     4\t> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n     5\t> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n     6\t> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n     7\t> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n     8\t> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n     9\t> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n    10\t> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n    11\t\n    12\t## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n    13\t\n    14\tBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n    15\t\n    16\t1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n    17\t2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n    18\t3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n    19\t   word for it is already given.\n    20\t4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n    21\t   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n    22\t5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n    23\t   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n    24\t\n    25\t## 1. Goal (end to end)\n    26\t\n    27\tEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\n    28\tnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\n    29\tany one step's own score.\n    30\t\n    31\t## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n    32\t\n    33\t**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n    34\t\n    35\tThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n    36\t\n    37\t- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n    38\t  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n    39\t  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n    40\t  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n    41\t  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n    42\t- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n    43\t  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n    44\t  nothing at all and were never judged.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Evidence:**\n    47\t\n    48\t| Evidence | Content | Source |\n    49\t|---|---|---|\n    50\t| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n    51\t| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n    52\t| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n    53\t| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n    54\t\n    55\tAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n    56\t\n    57\t## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n    58\t\n    59\t| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n    60\t|---|---|---|\n    61\t| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n    62\t| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n    63\t| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n    64\t| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n    65\t| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n    66\t| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n    67\t| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n    68\t| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n    69\t\n   428\t  predicted to move an answer by a blind second reader);\n   429\t- a same-news comparison from established libraries (D611: underpowered, and no unread week left).\n   430\t\n   431\tThe council's reversible decisions on Alex's page are recorded in D606 and D607.\n   432\t\n   433\t**The one next task (D665–D675): read the release comparison's six draws when they finish, with the council-reviewed tools**\n   434\t(`docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md` §1.4–§1.6; `DESIGN-1.6.md` v7; D675).\n   435\t\n   436\t- **Done:**\n   437\t  - stage 0 and slice 2;\n   438\t  - the full run, six draws, launched together at 22:36 on 2026-11-17 under `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/`;\n   439\t  - every reading instrument built and passed by the council before any output was read: reading tools in round 5, the §1.6 tools in\n   440\t    round 10; the scorer hardened through Codex rounds 11–21 (D675); 101 stage0 tests, 75 mutants on the reading tools.\n   441\t- **Result, 2026-11-19 (diagnostic, 5 draws; Alex stopped new-1).** The new system loses on the release comparison.\n   442\t  - Of 32 key matters, the new system serves 2–3 and the old one 10 (a = 0, b = 7–8). The controls pass.\n   443\t  - Even a perfect new-1 could not reverse it.\n   444\t  - The new libraries miss the core revenue, margin and capex matters.\n   445\t  - Details: `docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md`, `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/`.\n   446\t  - **The next task:** find why the new system's questions miss those matters, from the stored traces, at no cost, before any new run.\n   447\t- **(Superseded) When all six draws end, in this order:**\n   448\t  1. `eligibility.py`: six complete draws, launched within 1 h, sends within 72 h.\n   449\t  2. `mapping.py export`, then `read`, `third`, `result`.\n   450\t  3. `mark_cards.py deck`, then `mark`, `debate 1`, `debate 2`, `readings`.\n     1\t{\n     2\t \"note\": \"DIAGNOSTIC, not a release verdict: five finished draws (new-1 stopped after its one redo); a matter is served by a system when it is served in at least 2 of that system's finished draws (both of new-2 and new-3; 2 of 3 old)\",\n     3\t \"draws\": [\n     4\t  \"new-2\",\n     5\t  \"new-3\",\n     6\t  \"old-1\",\n     7\t  \"old-2\",\n     8\t  \"old-3\"\n     9\t ],\n    10\t \"N\": 32,\n    11\t \"margin_rule\": 5,\n    12\t \"counting 1\": {\n    13\t  \"a (new only)\": 0,\n    14\t  \"b (old only)\": 7,\n    15\t  \"served by new\": 3,\n    16\t  \"served by old\": 10,\n    17\t  \"both\": 3,\n    18\t  \"served_new\": [\n    19\t   \"M13\",\n    20\t   \"M15\",\n    21\t   \"M31\"\n    22\t  ],\n    23\t  \"served_old\": [\n    24\t   \"M04\",\n    25\t   \"M06\",\n    26\t   \"M10\",\n    27\t   \"M11\",\n    28\t   \"M13\",\n    29\t   \"M15\",\n    30\t   \"M17\",\n    31\t   \"M18\",\n    32\t   \"M19\",\n    33\t   \"M31\"\n    34\t  ]\n    35\t },\n    36\t \"counting 2\": {\n    37\t  \"a (new only)\": 0,\n    38\t  \"b (old only)\": 8,\n    39\t  \"served by new\": 2,\n    40\t  \"served by old\": 10,\n    41\t  \"both\": 2,\n    42\t  \"served_new\": [\n    43\t   \"M13\",\n    44\t   \"M15\"\n    45\t  ],\n    46\t  \"served_old\": [\n    47\t   \"M04\",\n    48\t   \"M06\",\n    49\t   \"M10\",\n    50\t   \"M11\",\n    51\t   \"M13\",\n    52\t   \"M15\",\n    53\t   \"M17\",\n    54\t   \"M18\",\n    55\t   \"M19\",\n    56\t   \"M31\"\n    57\t  ]\n    58\t },\n    59\t \"controls\": {\n    60\t  \"plants marked unsupported or insufficient\": 6,\n    61\t  \"plants\": 6,\n    62\t  \"supported controls marked supported\": 4,\n    63\t  \"supported controls\": 4,\n    64\t  \"repeats the same\": 3,\n    65\t  \"repeats\": 3\n    66\t },\n    67\t \"distinct bets per draw\": {\n    68\t  \"new-2\": 33,\n    69\t  \"new-3\": 41,\n    70\t  \"old-1\": 45,\n    71\t  \"old-2\": 41,\n    72\t  \"old-3\": 46\n    73\t }\n    74\t}\nDIAGNOSTIC\neligibility.json\nlibrary-L1.json\nlibrary-L2.json\nlibrary-L3.json\nlibrary-L5.json\nlibrary-L6.json\nmap-L1-claude.txt\nmap-L1-codex.txt\nmap-L2-claude.txt\nmap-L2-codex.txt\nmap-L3-claude.txt\nmap-L3-codex.txt\nmap-L5-claude.txt\nmap-L5-codex.txt\nmap-L6-claude.txt\nmap-L6-codex.txt\nmapping.json\nthird\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-1:\nlaunch.lock\npreconditions.log\nrun.json\nrun.json.bak-20261119-before-single-item\nstep1\nstep1-item-365\nstep1-patched\nstep1-redo\nstep1-redo.log\nstep1.log\nstep2\nstep2.log\n\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1:\nlaunch.lock\npreconditions.log\nprod\nprod.log\nrun.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
