{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '4107,4134p;5546,5602p;5835,5849p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,100p'; nl -ba clean-arch/PRD.md | sed -n '248,273p;593,613p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '4107,4134p;5546,5602p;5835,5849p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,100p'; nl -ba clean-arch/PRD.md | sed -n '248,273p;593,613p'\"","aggregated_output":"  4107\t## D382 · 2026-11-08 · Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason\n  4108\t\n  4109\t- Alex: \"我觉得财务类型不应该是thesis，而更多的是条件。观点应该是独特的view，而不是喊出来的数字，除非有理由 - 这个理由恰恰才是观点\". On the\n  4110\t  recommendation to keep a useful company figure no view takes as a condition of the company, he replied \"好\". Record:\n  4111\t  `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §§16–17.\n  4112\t\n  4113\t## D383 · 2026-11-08 · D209 amended again: a material statement no thesis takes is kept unlinked and linked later\n  4114\t\n  4115\t- Alex chose \"先存着，有观点再挂\": a statement the model judges useful but no thesis takes yet is kept in the company's record, linked when\n  4116\t  a related thesis opens; what the closing check rejects is still dropped, including the cash flow he ruled out. Amends D209 beyond D382.\n  4117\t  Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §27.\n  4118\t\n  4119\t## D384 · 2026-11-08 · Clean Step 1 opens only the big matters, by the signed standard as the frozen gold applies it\n  4120\t\n  4121\t- Alex chose \"按金标：只开大事\": a thesis opens only for the standard's reasons (an obligation the company takes on, its main product's\n  4122\t  next node, a policy step, a checkable shared quantity); another company's single project, partnership or product line is evidence.\n  4123\t  The reader-based small/fragment line gives way to must_open covered and must_not not opened. Class A (main-driver quantity) stays\n  4124\t  out under D382. Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §36.\n  4125\t\n  4126\t## D385 · 2026-11-08 · Target prices and valuation conclusions are not kept\n  4127\t\n  4128\t- Alex, 2026-11-08: \"留 EPS 预测，丢目标价\" (LOG §11), then, asked whether it overrides the signed standard's \"孤零零的目标价可选；带推导的\n  4129\t  条件估值仍是辅助\" (D243 #4), chose \"目标价和估值结论都不留\": a target price or valuation conclusion anyone draws is not kept; the\n  4130\t  estimates it rests on are kept on their own. The frozen standard page and golden-v5 are not edited (D261, D262); the two valuation\n  4131\t  entries golden-v5 marks supporting are disclosed as a known conflict with every score (D373). Record: LOG §39.\n  4132\t\n  4133\t## D386 · 2026-11-08 · Acceptance on fresh articles read by readers against the source\n  4134\t\n  5546\t## D489 · 2026-11-14 · The fresh week's result: not clear by the rule, no system chosen; the company's main numbers as questions goes to Alex (council consensus)\n  5547\t\n  5548\t- **Run** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md`): 2026-09-22..28, 235 articles, one draw a system from an empty library\n  5549\t  (the clean draw after D488, no network loss); $4.69 for the step (ceiling $8).\n  5550\t- **Readings, two blind reader families:**\n  5551\t  - A: of the five big matters both families listed, production covers 4 and the clean path 2. The clean path lacks FY2027 revenue, FY2028\n  5552\t    revenue and the FY2028 gross margin: its stored reasoning names the request's do-not-open sentence for financial measures on those\n  5553\t    articles (D382, D384); 145 kept statements of the company's own figures have no question. Production lacks the supply commitments (its\n  5554\t    one statement on the $279 billion sits under the credit-support question). Questions worth holding: clean 6 of 7; production 8 or 9 of\n  5555\t    15 (3 duplicates and 3 trivia by both families).\n  5556\t  - B: last judgements supported by both families: clean 6 of 7, production 10 of 15; unsupported by both: one, production's data-center\n  5557\t    revenue (a growth rate the judge allowed itself). The Codex reader parted from the separate reader on two of the four supported\n  5558\t    controls, both production's, with reasons that stand as a disagreement; B at this size cannot rank the systems.\n  5559\t- **The rule written before reading (LEAN-LOG §2), as written:** production meets the first half (two more matters), not the second (19\n  5560\t  points lower on B): **not clear; no system is chosen.**\n  5561\t- **Source check ($0, asked by the council):** a narrow door on the clean path (a question only where the item holds the company's outlook and\n  5562\t  a market expectation for the same measure and period) covers 0 of 7 articles for FY2027 revenue, 2 of 8 for FY2028 revenue, 1 of 2 for the\n  5563\t  margin: dropped. The readers' reason is \"main driver\" in all 24 of their revenue and margin entries; production's data-center revenue\n  5564\t  question was opened from a bare reported figure.\n  5565\t- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mw-codex-11.md`, `mw-codex-12.md`): \"不选择系统，向 Alex 提交财务问题的产品选择；选项应包括单独追踪\n  5566\t  主要数字、维持现状，以及保留观点原则但让相关财务资料可见、可用，并如实说明本周证据的限制。\"\n  5567\t- **To Alex (his D382 and D384; nothing is sent before he answers):** (1) test questions on the company's main numbers on the new system\n  5568\t  (Claude's lean, a lean only); (2) keep the rule as it is and record the three matters as by design; (3) keep the view principle and make the\n  5569\t  kept figures visible and used when a view they bear on is tracked.\n  5570\t\n  5571\t## D490 · 2026-11-14 · Alex opens a test: the new system may open questions on the company's revenue and margin\n  5572\t\n  5573\t- **Asked** (after D489, his reply to this exact question): \"这一周的对比显示：现行系统会为营收、毛利率开问题；新系统按你之前定的规则（D382：财务数字是条件，不是\n  5574\t  问题）不开，所以两组盲评读者都列出的 5 件大事里它少了 3 件（FY2027 营收、FY2028 营收、FY2028 毛利率），145 条公司财务数字没有被任何判断读到。新系统接下来怎么处理营收\n  5575\t  和毛利率？\" Options: test opening such questions (recommended); keep the rule; open none but use the figures.\n  5576\t- **Alex:** \"试开这类问题 (Recommended)\". The option as shown to him: \"先在这周已存的文章上花几美分试：能否开出这 3 个问题，同时不乱开、不重复；通过后再跑第二个没用过的\n  5577\t  新鲜周。会改变你的 D382/D384。历史上类似的放开曾多开 7 个不该开的问题（那次同时改了三处）。\"\n  5578\t- **Decided:** a test arm of clean Step 1 is opened (a new version of the frozen c8 request, for this test only; c8 stays the adopted\n  5579\t  request until a result is adopted). D382 and D384 stay in force for the adopted path; the arm departs from them on one point, the\n  5580\t  company's main numbers as questions. First a probe of a few cents on the stored week's states, with its lines and stop condition written\n  5581\t  before any send and a council round before the send (AGENTS §7.3); the second fresh week runs only if the probe meets its lines.\n  5582\t\n  5583\t## D491 · 2026-11-14 · The revenue-and-margin test arm (c20) fails its probe's first step and is stopped; what next goes to Alex (council consensus)\n  5584\t\n  5585\t- **Probe** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/PROBE-DESIGN.md`, `RESULT.md`; lines written before the send, two blind audits of\n  5586\t  the wording, council rounds 13 to 15): ten stored states of the fresh week, c8 and c20, three sends each, 60 valid sends, $1.02.\n  5587\t- **Result, two blind reader families beside Claude:** c20 opens fiscal 2027 revenue (9 of 9 sends on its cases) and the fiscal 2028 gross\n  5588\t  margin (6 of 6); fiscal 2028 revenue in 13 of 15, seven of them as a growth rate with no base year, which the readers count differently (2\n  5589\t  of 5 cases against 3 of 5; three needed); the named figures are kept and linked; no question on EPS, a quarter or another company; none\n  5590\t  twice in one answer; none from a bare reported figure. **It fails on suppression:** on the article where c8 opens the Vera Rubin question\n  5591\t  in 2 of 3 sends, c20 opens it in 0 of 3 and files the statement under the new revenue question. The supply-commitments control was absent\n  5592\t  (c8 1 of 3).\n  5593\t- **Cause not settled:** the reasoning gives the article's missing shipment date and the revenue question as a ready home side by side; c8's\n  5594\t  one non-opening send gives the same date reason. Also seen: 31 of the 97 statements linked to the new questions carry no company figure\n  5595\t  (five AMD statements under NVIDIA's revenue on one article).\n  5596\t- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mw-codex-16.md`): \"c20 按预定条件失败并停止；推荐先核查已保留财务资料的实际可见和使用路径，同时把产品题缺失的日期与收入\n  5597\t  归档两种可能原因如实交给 Alex。\"\n  5598\t- **Decided:** c20 is not adopted and not carried further; step two and the second fresh week are not run; c8 stays the adopted request and\n  5599\t  D382 and D384 stay as they are. The arm's files stay as the record. **To Alex:** stop the question-opening line and look at how the kept\n  5600\t  figures can be seen and used (the council's and Claude's lean), or one more arm that limits what a main-number question takes as\n  5601\t  evidence, measured on unread cases.\n  5602\t\n  5835\t## D505 · 2026-11-15 · Alex: the kept financial figures should reach the judgements of related questions; first a $0 check\n  5836\t\n  5837\t- **Asked** (after D504, his reply to this exact question, several answers allowed): \"对公司的主要财务数字（营收、毛利率的指引、市场预期、实际业绩），新系统已经存下来了，但现在既不展示也不判断。\n  5838\t  你希望读者能用它们做什么？（可多选）\" Options: reach the judgements of related questions (recommended); be looked up in a table; tracked questions\n  5839\t  with judgements; none for now.\n  5840\t- **Alex:** \"进入相关问题的判断 (Recommended)\" (the only option he chose). The option as shown: \"符合你定的规则：财务数字是观点的证据，不单独开成问题。第一步不花钱（$0）：检查现有问题做\n  5841\t  判断时，有没有系统存了、本该用到、却没送进去的财务数字。有就报给你，没有就停。\"\n  5842\t- **Decided:** the company's kept financial figures are evidence for the judgements of related questions; they are not opened as\n  5843\t  questions of their own (D382 and D384 stand), and he did not choose the table or tracked financial questions. The first step is a\n  5844\t  $0 check on the stored fresh-week run of the new system: for each existing question's judgement, is a kept financial figure it\n  5845\t  should have received absent from its request. A finding is reported to him; none ends the line. Nothing is sent to a model;\n  5846\t  nothing changes in the system by this check.\n  5847\t\n  5848\t## D506 · 2026-11-15 · The delivery check: one kept financial fact did not reach a question it bears on; six open leads; nothing is built on it (council consensus)\n  5849\t\n     1\t# Lean step 2: one fresh week, one draw a system — result (D487, D488), 2026-11-14\n     2\t\n     3\t**Answer: by the rule written before reading, the difference is not clear.** Production covers two more of the five big matters both reader\n     4\tfamilies listed (4 against 2), which meets the rule's first half; its share of last judgements both families call supported is lower by 19\n     5\tpoints (10 of 15 against 6 of 7), more than the one in ten the second half allows. Each half has one named cause. The first is one rule: the\n     6\tthree matters the clean path lacks are the company's own revenue and margin, which its request forbids as questions (D382). The second rests\n     7\tmostly on one reader family: Codex failed 2 of the 4 judgements a separate reader had confirmed as supported, both of them production's;\n     8\tboth families call only one judgement unsupported, production's data-center revenue.\n     9\t\n    10\tMaterial: 2026-09-22..28, 235 articles (232 never sent by any run), each system one draw from an empty library: the clean path\n    11\t`poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week-r2/c1` (after D488), production `…/week/p1`. Readers: Codex (read-only) and Claude subagents, blind\n    12\tto the systems and to each other; the keys are outside the repository. Model cost of the step (the one-day slice, production's draw, the\n    13\tclean draw and its two stopped attempts): $4.69. One draw each: every count below is one draw.\n    14\t\n    15\t## What each system holds at the week's end (counted from the stored runs)\n    16\t\n    17\t| | clean c1 | production p1 |\n    18\t|---|---|---|\n    19\t| questions opened | 7 | 15 |\n    20\t| statements written | 569, from 182 articles | 673, from 186 articles |\n    21\t| thrown away for having no question | 0 | 278 |\n    22\t| kept (after joining repeats) | 569 (314) | 385 |\n    23\t| kept with no question: no judgement reads them | 389 | 0 |\n    24\t| links to questions | 196 | 449 (126 on FY2027 total revenue, 94 on data-center revenue) |\n    25\t| judgements | 37 | 72 |\n    26\t\n    27\t## A. Big questions (40 sampled articles; eight matters, five listed by both families)\n    28\t\n    29\t| matter | listed by | clean c1 | production p1 |\n    30\t|---|---|---|---|\n    31\t| M01 FY2027 revenue (total or data center) | both | **missed** | opened (v2, v4) |\n    32\t| M02 FY2028 revenue | both | **missed** | opened (v3, v5) |\n    33\t| M03 FY2028 gross margin against the 72%–73% outlook | both | **missed** | opened (v10) |\n    34\t| M04 supply and capacity purchase commitments ($279B at Q2) | both | opened (clean-2) | **missed** |\n    35\t| M05 Beijing's approval of RTX Pro 5500 purchases | both | opened (clean-7) | opened (v14, v15) |\n    36\t| M06 FY2027 gross margin | one | missed | missed |\n    37\t| M07 Vera Rubin revenue shipments in Q3 | one | opened (Claude) / a later deadline that does not settle Q3 (Codex) | the same split |\n    38\t| M08 AMD's 2027 data-center revenue | one | missed | missed |\n    39\t\n    40\tThe families give the same status on 14 of 16 cells and on all ten cells of M01–M05. **Covered, of the five: clean 2, production 4.**\n    41\t\n    42\tEach opened question, read beside the article it was opened from:\n    43\t\n    44\t| | clean c1 (7) | production p1 (15) |\n    45\t|---|---|---|\n    46\t| worth holding | 6 (both families) | 9 (Codex) / 8 (Claude) |\n    47\t| trivia | 1: the Hugging Face purchase closing | 3: \"tech companies' AI spending\" (nothing settles it), the Hugging Face price as a commitment, the Anthropic IPO stake |\n    48\t| duplicate of another of its own | 0 | 3 by both: FY2028 growth of FY2028 revenue, Rubin by end-2027 of Rubin by January 2027, the second RTX Pro 5500 question; Claude adds data-center revenue of total revenue |\n    49\t\n    50\tChecked by Claude against the stored runs:\n    51\t- Production has no supply-commitments question: its one kept statement on the $279 billion is linked to the credit-support question (v1).\n    52\t- The clean path's three misses are its rule at work. On each article where production opened v2, v3, v4, v5 and v10, the clean draw's\n    53\t  stored reasoning names the request's sentence \"Do not open a thesis about … a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for\n    54\t  any period, on its own\", opens nothing and keeps the statements; 109 of 235 steps' reasoning names that sentence. The request sends such\n    55\t  figures to \"an open thesis about its revenue or earnings path\", which nothing in an empty library is: 145 kept statements of the company's\n    56\t  own figures (from 67 articles) have no question, among them the 70% growth outlook for fiscal 2028, which the articles set against the 45%\n    57\t  the Street had modelled (14 statements, 14 articles), and gross-margin figures of 71% to 73% (11 statements, 9 articles).\n    58\t- Both families call the Hugging Face purchase small (both systems opened a question on it). It is listed as the readers gave it; D389's\n    59\t  size line is for unsigned obligations in its own test and does not rule on this question (council round 11).\n    60\t\n    61\t## B. Judgement support (26 items: 22 real last judgements, 4 planted from earlier judgements)\n    62\t\n    63\t| | Codex | Claude |\n    64\t|---|---|---|\n    65\t| planted wrong judgements caught | 4 of 4 | 4 of 4 |\n    66\t| supported controls passed (confirmed first by a separate reader) | **2 of 4** | 4 of 4 |\n    67\t| clean c1 (7): supported / unsupported / insufficient | 6 / 1 / 0 | 7 / 0 / 0 |\n    68\t| production p1 (15) | 10 / 2 / 3 | 14 / 1 / 0 |\n    69\t\n    70\tSupported by both families: **clean 6 of 7 (86%), production 10 of 15 (67%)**. Unsupported by both: one, production's data-center revenue (v4):\n    71\tits rung is reached by a fourth-quarter growth of about 25% that the judge itself calls an allowance; no shown piece gives the rate, and the\n    72\tshown 18% lands a rung lower. Called not supported by Codex alone: the clean path's credit-support total (a cap read as the amount);\n    73\tproduction's credit-support total and its first RTX Pro 5500 question (**both are confirmed supported controls**), the Hugging Face amount and\n    74\tthe Anthropic stake (both also called trivia in A). Cited statements with a field error: one in each system (a quarter mislabelled; \"more than\n    75\tdoubling to $115 billion\" written as \"will exceed\").\n    76\t\n    77\t## The rule, applied as written (LEAN-LOG §2)\n    78\t\n    79\t- First half (A): production covers two more of the matters both families listed. Met by production.\n    80\t- Second half (B): its share of judgements both families call supported is lower by 19 points, more than one in ten. Not met.\n    81\t- **Verdict: not clear. The next small step targets the largest difference observed, not a choice of system.**\n    82\t\n    83\tWhat weakens each half: A's three-matter gap is one sentence of the clean request, a product rule (D382), not a capability. B compares 7\n    84\tjudgements with 15, so one judgement is 14 points for the clean path; the gap comes from one family, which parted from the separate reader on two of the four supported controls, both production items, with\n    85\treasons that stand as a disagreement (a guarantee cap read as the amount; permission for two named firms read from \"some firms\"). As a\n    86\tsensitivity note only: with those two counted as the separate reader read them, production would stand at 12 of 15; the rule's count stays\n    87\t10 of 15. B at this size cannot say which system judges better.\n    88\t\n    89\t## The largest difference observed\n    90\t\n    91\tHow each system treats the company's own revenue and margin: three of the five matters, 145 kept statements no judgement reads on one side;\n    92\ton the other, the same matters opened, with two or three duplicates among them and 126 statements piled on one question.\n    93\t\n    94\t## The source check the council asked for ($0, council round 11): do the articles hold a dispute, or only a number?\n    95\t\n    96\tClaude's first candidate for a next step was a narrow door on the clean path: open a revenue or margin question only when the item holds both\n    97\tthe company's own outlook and a stated market expectation for the same measure and period. Read against every article the readers listed\n    98\tfor M01–M03 and every article production opened its five such questions from:\n    99\t\n   100\t| matter | articles | hold such a pair | what they hold instead |\n   248\t### What the model decides\n   249\t\n   250\tFor each statement an analyst would note, one of four results:\n   251\t\n   252\t1. **Evidence for an open thesis.** The statement is linked to every open thesis it informs, with the reason.\n   253\t2. **A new thesis.** Only for a big matter, by one of the standard's four reasons: an obligation the company takes on, its main\n   254\t   product's next node, a policy stage, or a checkable shared quantity (D384; Alex: \"按金标：只开大事\"). Another company's single\n   255\t   project, partnership or product line is evidence, not a thesis. A new thesis carries the entity (supplied by code), the question,\n   256\t   the outcome to track and the period when known (Alex, 2026-11-06); a meaningful matter may open without a known decision date when\n   257\t   later developments can settle it.\n   258\t3. **A material statement no thesis takes yet.** It is kept in the company's record without links and linked when a thesis that\n   259\t   covers it opens (D383; Alex: \"先存着，有观点再挂\").\n   260\t4. **Nothing.** What the closing check rejects is dropped with its reason, never parked.\n   261\t\n   262\tThree of Alex's rules shape the reading:\n   263\t- **A financial figure is a condition, not a thesis** (D382; Alex: \"我觉得财务类型不应该是thesis，而更多的是条件。观点应该是独特的view，而不是喊出来的数字，除非有理由 - 这个理由恰恰才是观点\").\n   264\t  A statement of the company's own useful figures lists them, and code checks each value against a verified passage. Those figures are\n   265\t  evidence for the judgements of related questions (D505).\n   266\t- **Target prices and valuation conclusions are not kept**; the estimates they rest on are (D385).\n   267\t- **Lean cautious, catch the increment** (D243): most of an item is common knowledge and is not kept; new information that can change\n   268\t  an answer is never missed.\n   269\t\n   270\tStep 1 decides in the same reading whether a matter is already tracked; there is no separate thesis-routing stage. That is a choice\n   271\tof this design, and where it fails it fails at opening (section 8).\n   272\t\n   273\t### Output\n   593\t- NO THESIS YET: if no open or newly proposed thesis covers a statement you judge material, and the matter is not big enough by\n   594\t  its own scale to merit a thesis (section 3), return it with empty links; it is kept without links.\n   595\t- CONDITION: a statement of the company's own financial figures (a reported result or balance, its guidance, or a named party's\n   596\t  or consensus estimate) lists its useful figures in figures. Its results, guidance and estimates, margins included, inform an open thesis about its revenue or earnings\n   597\t  path when they bear on that path; a different period is not on its own a reason to leave them unlinked. When no open or new\n   598\t  thesis covers it, its links stay empty. A figure is useful when it can change what an analyst\n   599\t  expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position: a retailer's quarterly\n   600\t  same-store sales, an airline's guidance for next year's unit costs and analysts' consensus earnings for a bank are; a cash-rich\n   601\t  company's cash balance or cash flow usually changes none of these when the item ties it to nothing, while a heavily indebted\n   602\t  firm's cash burn changes its credit risk. The share price, a target price and other companies' figures are never conditions.\n   603\t- Link one statement to every thesis it informs, and to none that its own relevance says it does not inform; use the narrowest\n   604\t  relevant thesis only when choosing between theses that cover the same thing.\n   605\t- Match by the underlying question or outcome, subject and scope, and time when relevant, not by word overlap. A different wording,\n   606\t  source, forecast or direction alone does not make a new thesis. Related questions can be separate when their outcomes matter\n   607\t  independently.\n   608\t- Do not exclude evidence solely because it concerns a related period, population or product variant. Assess whether it can inform\n   609\t  the open question, preserving the difference in the record. Do not present a forecast for a later year as a forecast for the\n   610\t  thesis's year. If another open thesis covers the evidence more directly, consider that thesis as well; do not assume different\n   611\t  periods are automatically the same thesis or automatically unrelated.\n   612\t\n   613\tExamples of linking evidence to research:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
