O anchor investment.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:18:{\"matter\": \"M18\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No FY2027 gross margin question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:19:{\"matter\": \"M19\", \"status\": \"opened\", \"ids\": [\"Q32\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Same closing outcome; Q32's deadline is 2027-12-31 rather than 2027-06-30.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:20:{\"matter\": \"M20\", \"status\": \"opened\", \"ids\": [\"Q20\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Q20 asks whether the financing arrangement with Blackstone and others is signed by end-2027; it names Apollo rather than Goldman and does not mention residual-value support. Match is uncertain.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:25:{\"matter\": \"M25\", \"status\": \"broader\", \"ids\": [\"Q39\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Q39 resolves on any DOJ decision on Groq, including closure; enforcement is only one way to settle it.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:26:{\"matter\": \"M26\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No question on the stage of EU review of Hugging Face.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:27:{\"matter\": \"M27\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No question on the outstanding Hugging Face obligation amount.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:28:{\"matter\": \"M28\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No question on the stage of US antitrust review of Hugging Face.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:31:{\"matter\": \"M31\", \"status\": \"opened\", \"ids\": [\"Q1\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Same 10-K aggregate of guarantees and credit support for AI cloud partners at FY2027 year-end.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt:32:{\"matter\": \"M32\", \"status\": \"opened\", \"ids\": [\"Q30\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Same 10-K figure for cloud-service capacity commitments to AI cloud partners at FY2027 year-end.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:4:{\"matter\": \"M04\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No hyperscaler capex question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:6:{\"matter\": \"M06\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No NVIDIA data-center revenue question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:10:{\"matter\": \"M10\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No FY2028 gross margin question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:11:{\"matter\": \"M11\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No FY2028 total revenue question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:12:{\"matter\": \"M12\", \"status\": \"broader\", \"ids\": [\"Q26\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"The Ohio lease backstop is folded into Q26's aggregate of residual value guaranties and data-center lease credit support.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:17:{\"matter\": \"M17\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Anthropic IPO anchor investment question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:18:{\"matter\": \"M18\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No FY2027 gross margin question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:19:{\"matter\": \"M19\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Hugging Face acquisition question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:20:{\"matter\": \"M20\", \"status\": \"broader\", \"ids\": [\"Q26\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Q26 measures aggregate residual value guaranties at FY2027 year-end; it reflects signing only indirectly, with a different date and shape.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:25:{\"matter\": \"M25\", \"status\": \"broader\", \"ids\": [\"Q32\"], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"Q32 resolves on any formal DOJ resolution of the Groq review (closing or enforcement) by 2027-01-31; enforcement is a subset.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:26:{\"matter\": \"M26\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Hugging Face EU review question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:27:{\"matter\": \"M27\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Hugging Face obligation question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:28:{\"matter\": \"M28\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No Hugging Face US antitrust question.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:31:{\"matter\": \"M31\", \"status\": \"opened\", \"ids\": [\"Q1\"], \"main_outcome\": true, \"note\": \"Q1 asks for total guarantees and credit support to AI cloud customers at FY2027 year-end per the 10-K. Q26 covers the lease-guarantee portion only.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt:32:{\"matter\": \"M32\", \"status\": \"missed\", \"ids\": [], \"main_outcome\": null, \"note\": \"No question on cloud-service/neocloud capacity commitments. Q6 covers supply purchases, and Q1's credit support may only partly touch the backstops.\"}\nL3--M31--Q1--claude.json\nL3--M31--Q1--codex.json\nL5--M31--Q1--claude.json\nL5--M31--Q1--codex.json\nL6--M25--Q43--claude.json\nL6--M25--Q43--codex.json\nL6--M31--Q2--claude.json\nL6--M31--Q2--codex.json\nC001-claude.json\nC001-codex.json\nC002-claude.json\nC002-codex.json\nC003-claude.json\nC003-codex.json\nC004-claude.json\nC004-codex.json\nC005-claude.json\nC005-codex.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-2:\ncases\ncases.log\njudge\njudge-inputs.json\njudge.log\nladder\nladder.log\nlaunch.lock\npreconditions.log\nrun.json\nstep1\nstep1.log\nstep2\nstep2.log\n\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-3:\ncases\ncases.log\njudge\njudge-inputs.json\njudge.log\nladder\nladder.log\nlaunch.lock\npreconditions.log\nrun.json\nstep1\nstep1.log\nstep2\nstep2.log\n     1\t# Run log: the release comparison (D665, D666)\n     2\t\n     3\tOne dated row per event and check, with numbers. Newest last.\n     4\t\n     5\t| When (2026-11-17) | Stage | Event | Numbers / outcome |\n     6\t|---|---|---|---|\n     7\t| — | plan | RUN-PLAN v1 written; council review started (Codex thread 01a1ebfe…, one Claude reviewer) | — |\n     8\t| 2026-11-17 | plan | Round 1: Codex NOT READY (5 points), Claude reviewer NOT READY (5 changes); every point checked against code (`triage-1.md`) | Blockers confirmed: Step 1 limits 300 calls / 8 h; ladder still luna; production ignores exclusions; judge stops at the last article; 15 s/article estimate wrong (measured 26–34 s) |\n     9\t| 2026-11-17 | plan | Census of inputs: 1,976 articles (357 warm-up, 1,619 scored); Step 1 failures in stored traces: 4 of 2,549, all dropped connections before the 11-15 network retry, 0 of 624 after | — |\n    10\t| 2026-11-17 | plan | RUN-PLAN v2 written (census moved to stage 0, company figures counted in N with the subgroup printed beside, exposure narrowing named, five code changes, rebased estimates); round 2 sent (Codex thread, fresh Claude reviewer) | — |\n    11\t| 2026-11-17 | plan | Round 2: Codex NOT READY, Claude reviewer NOT READY (7 changes); retry, binary-search and cost-curve findings checked against code and stored runs; lessons in ROUND-LOG.md; structural rule adopted (prose review stops at design level; build-level checked at the stage-0 freeze review) | — |\n    12\t| 2026-11-17 | plan | RUN-PLAN v3 written; round 3 sent (Codex thread, fresh Claude reviewer) | — |\n    13\t| 2026-11-17 | plan | Rounds 3–10: v3 to v9 (design-level review only from round 3; build-level items in freeze-review-notes.md). Claude reviewer READY at v7; Codex READY at round 10 on v9 and the decision text | D667 recorded (log, index, CURRENT_STATE) |\n    14\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Replay folders classified before any hit: two blind readers (Codex, Claude) both chose folder level, all 12 folders reads; frozen `stage0/replay-folders.json` (sha 0aa44d48…) | scored window by date: 08-31..09-20 (3 weeks, 720 articles before the census) |\n    15\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Census sample amended (D668, Codex AGREE): every kept article in the window; warm-up 07-01..08-30 unfiltered | — |\n    16\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Exposure census (`stage0/exposure_census.py`, 6 controls passed; 2 min; checkout, 5 worktrees, backups): under D667's frozen rule **720 of 720** window articles are reads | kept 0. Strict cause: superseded corpus states in the backups, two run-local corpus copies, `poc/corpus/items.sqlite`, and corpus-wide code-only censuses (source-loss, source-lineage) touch every article |\n    17\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Content-use look ($0, after the hits, not adopted): the week of 08-31 was processed end to end by the old system's seven-day runs (no-preseed worktree, 2026-11-05); 09-07 and 09-14 partly by the new system's 11-09 acceptance run and Step 2 councils | a property rule by folder misclassified gold and reader folders, so it is not usable; plan trigger \"N < 20 at the census\" → Alex |\n    18\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | D669 (Alex: \"只排除真被读过的，比9/7–9/20\"): read rule in `stage0/classify_reads.py` keeps **414 of 502** (09-07: 172 of 229; 09-14: 242 of 273); not-read locations: 8 storage, 18 pool lists, 14 code-only (all in the source-loss and source-provenance censuses); council check sent | — |\n    19\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Code D (`stage0/stage_a_astra.py`): 4 tests pass; 2 mutants caught as predicted (transport check off → a request reached the transport; build check off → 2 drifted requests sent); worst-case reserve $0.864 an astra attempt | `mutants-stage-a-astra.txt` |\n    20\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Codes A, C, D (launcher side) and E in `run_fresh.py` (+ `run_stage_b.py` forwards end_day): 33 launcher tests pass (30 existing + 3 new); 5 in-memory mutants caught as predicted, control passes | `mutants-run-fresh.txt`; open: a run_stage_b test for the end-day pass-through and the trailing-day proof |\n    21\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Read-rule check (Codex + Claude checker): 4 reader-shown articles added as reads (confirmed in the council sessions); 37 bulk-viewer-only articles kept excluded (split, safer course); **410 kept, frozen** (`stage0/kept-articles.json`, 172 + 238) | D670 |\n    22\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Matter census launched: 410 kept articles in 11 batches (35,35,35,35,32,40,40,40,40,40,38), two families, 22 closed sessions; Codex memory probe: no memory | prompts hashed in stage0/census/prompts.sha256 |\n    23\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Census reading done: 22 sessions, 0 void; Codex 164 questions (93 batch matters), Claude 205 (95); spot-read batch 07 side by side (well aligned) | — |\n    24\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Census merge → reconcile → 94 third-reader sessions → 38 entries; Codex council check found same-bet duplicates and an over-merge; dedup (both families) + blind adjudication of 10 pairs (20 sessions) | **N = 32** (7 company figures), `stage0/census/matters.json` frozen (D671); 2 split pairs disclosed |\n    25\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Committed 099f4a8 (Alex: \"你clean up提交\"); shared items DB built (92 excluded rows deleted, sha 75c28d3c…); two-entry input proof: 1,884 items 07-01..09-20, same set and order, controls pass; limits, verdict-rule.json and versions-manifest.json frozen | next: freeze review, then the slice |\n    26\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Size check (§1.7): v118's 14-day draws q1-q3 max judging request 114 KB / 29K input tokens; v34 end-state proxy 630 pieces (~500 KB, overstated: v34 linked wide) — watched, never a stop. Preflight (production, frozen v108 d1): A 2/2 schema refusals as stored, B 12/726 dropped (7 quote, 5 merged), C 0/170, D 0/43 — unchanged baseline | stage0/preflight-output.txt |\n    27\t| 2026-11-17 | stage 0 | Freeze review: Codex NOT READY, Claude reviewer NOT READY; fixes applied (per-pass check + test + 2 mutants, verdict rule completed sha 693911eb, card spec c930a860, launcher git-clean/ledger/redo); new judge size max 100 KB / 21.9K tokens; split on resequencing → D672 (Alex's word + Claude reviewer's conditions) | next: commit, re-freeze manifest, launch the slice |\n    28\t| 20:55 | slice | Launched s-new (clean, astra-frozen, ledger $10) and s-old (poc-v118, ledger $3), 07-01..07-07, on the shared items DB at 13bc220d | — |\n    29\t| 2026-11-17 21:00 | run | Alex: \"开始跑，需要用council loop 讨论结果\" — the full run starts as soon as the slice passes its checks (D672); results go to a council loop | — |\n    30\t| 22:05 | slice | s-old complete ($0.22). s-new stopped at the ladder: the shared ledger refused a $1.33 astra reservation against the slice's $10 guard (spent $2.86; 8 concurrent worst-case reservations ≈ $10.7). Diagnosis: guard sizing, a launcher parameter (plan §2: fix the launcher only, rerun). Before the stop: Step 1 98 articles ≈ 40 s and $0.011 each; Step 2 and cases complete (9 cases); 5 astra ladder sends answered, no wrapper refusal. Full-run guard $65 leaves room (≈ $23 spent + ≈ $11 reservations at that point) | rerun as slice-2, 07-01..07-03, guards $25 / $3 |\n    31\t| 2026-11-17 22:35 | slice-2 | Both draws complete (new \\$0.93, old \\$0.05). Checks: 1–4 PASS at once; 5 and 6 failed first by the checks' own error. Old's 3 extra items are copies merged into their originals (not extracted), and day-end judgements carry `day:<date>`. Corrected and rerun: **all six PASS** (39 articles, 42.1 s and \\$0.0084 each, every ladder pass astra, same 39 items in order, a day state reads back) | stage0/slice-2-checks.txt |\n    32\t| 2026-11-17 22:36 | run | **Full run launched:** new-1..3 (clean, astra-frozen, guard \\$65 each) and old-1..3 (poc-v118, guard \\$25 each), 07-01..09-20, on the shared items DB, all six within one minute (D667 timing), at commit 4c66408f | monitor armed (stops, crashes, component changes, progress every 100 attempts / 7 days) |\n    33\t| 22:41 | reading tools | mapping.py (3 tests), mark_cards.py (4 tests), build_cards.py type field; card form check (D673): round 1 named two rung annotations (removed) and a truncation artefact of the check itself; round 2 named only the systems' own structure (rung counts, library sizes), disclosed | stage0/blinding-check-codex*.md |\n    34\t| 23:03 | check | six draws running; spend new 0.43–0.45, old 0.91–1.08; my own mistake: a status check tried to count rows in a live Step 1 trace (AGENTS §9: never open a live run's databases); refused by the classifier, not repeated; status is read from run.json and the ledgers only | run/ |\n    35\t| 23:24 | card form check (D673), rounds 3–4 on the new card (request context, own opening place, numbered answers) | round 3 named one form element: the answer step's third annotation form ('the amount last reported when the question opened'); the annotation filter is now the closed set of ladder_step's three suffixes (484 stored conditions, 0 left annotated). Round 4 named only content (rung counts, theme counts, library size): closed, disclosed with the result | stage0/blinding-check-codex-3.md, -4.md |\n    36\t| 23:37 | reading-tools council, rounds 2–4 | round 2–3 both readers not ready (eligibility, mapping validation, publishers, debate, plants, split readings, card context); round 4: Claude ready to read, Codex 3 more (key-verified card flags, reconciled attempt log, theme rungs), fixed; 47 tests, 39 mutants + 5 controls as predicted; §1.6 design v2 sent with round 5 | D675; tools-review-codex-2..4.md; DESIGN-1.6.md |\n    37\t| 00:06 | §1.6 design rounds 5–7 → v6; reading tools committed (c3704776, 802f2b08) | both readers: design faithful after v6's small fixes; built eligibility inputs, D400 code check, printed-beside quantities, diagnostic export (54 tests, 43 mutants + 6 controls); three builders started in parallel for D400 reader lines, Step 2 lines, D431 at 07-14 (new files only, fake readers) | DESIGN-1.6.md v6; D675 |\n    38\t| 00:29 | three §1.6 tools built (D400 reader lines 7 tests, Step 2 lines 10, D431 6; each with mutants on scratch copies) | finding: Step 2 line 3 as v6 defines it is predetermined (group_text drops later reports' tier/stated day/period/speaker; v6 counts them; c1: 78/79 groups) while the product's judge reads each member's full record (PRD §6; 741 and 1,127 same-claim notes in c1/p1 requests); sent to the council as round 8 with the tools | tools-review-brief-8.md |\n    39\t| 01:02 | §1.6 tools pass the council (round 10, Codex READY; Claude round 9 points fixed) | every instrument D672 requires is built and reviewed before any output: reading tools (round 5) and §1.6 tools (round 10); 92 stage0 tests; CURRENT_STATE next task = the reading order once the six draws end | f2cbfcfa |\n    40\t| 01:20 | old-1, old-2 complete | old-1 $9.83, old-2 $8.60, no stop; old-3 near the end; the new draws still in Step 1 (about $2.8 each) | run/ |\n    41\t| 01:21 | old-3 complete | $8.83, no stop; the three old draws total $27.26 against $25 guards each (not a budget); the new draws are in Step 1 | run/ |\n    42\t| 13:11 | reading chain dry run end to end on the slice ($0, fake reader) | every step joins; verdict 'too small' as ordered; gap fixed: printed-beside quantities now computed for invalid and too-small verdicts too | stage0/chain_dry_run.py |\n    43\t\n    44\t- 2026-11-18 13:59: The scorer and the chain rebuild were hardened through Codex rounds 11–22. Round 22 returned READY.\n    45\t  - The verdict is computed only on a snapshot rebuilt from the primary data.\n    46\t  - Any derived file that differs from the rebuild is refused.\n    47\t  - Coverage: 101 stage0 tests; 75 mutants, all as predicted; the chain dry run passes (D675).\n    48\t  - The run is unchanged: old-1..3 finished; new-1..3 are in Step 1, at $16.2–17.0 each at 13:39.\n    49\t\n    50\t- 2026-11-18 18:12: new-2 finished Step 1 after 19 h 36 min. Its step1.log reads `status complete, error null, calls 1899`, and $21.14 was spent.\n    51\t  Step 2 then started at 18:12:37. Two figures to keep apart: `reserved_usd` 265.30 in the log is the running sum of what each call set\n    52\t  aside before it ran, while the ledger's spend is $21.14. new-1 and new-3 are still in Step 1.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
