trivia': 5, 'duplicate': 2, \"{'split': ['trivia', 'worth']}\": 1})\n{'Q13': {'worth': {'split': ['trivia', 'worth']}, 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-07-09'}, 'Q1': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'figure', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-07-01'}, 'Q32': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'figure', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-08-24'}, 'Q26': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-07-29'}, 'Q40': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-09-14'}, 'Q9': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported', 'type': 'figure', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-07-06'}, 'Q6': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported', 'type': 'figure', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-07-04'}, 'Q39': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': {'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']}, 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-09-10'}, 'Q20': {'worth': 'trivia', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-07-24'}}\nold-3 {'ids': 49, 'duplicates_both': 3, 'duplicates_split': 1} 40 Counter({'worth': 28, 'duplicate': 4, 'trivia': 4, \"{'split': ['worth', 'duplicate']}\": 2, \"{'split': ['worth', 'trivia']}\": 2})\n{'Q31': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'figure', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-08-06'}, 'Q1': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'figure', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-07-01'}, 'Q47': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': False, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-09-14'}, 'Q26': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': {'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']}, 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-07-28'}, 'Q6': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'figure', 'guardrail': False, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-07-04'}, 'Q32': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-08-07'}, 'Q9': {'worth': 'trivia', 'answer': {'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']}, 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-07-07'}, 'Q20': {'worth': {'split': ['worth', 'trivia']}, 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-07-24'}, 'Q40': {'worth': 'trivia', 'answer': 'unsupported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-08-29'}, 'Q13': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': False, 'opened': '2026-07-09'}, 'Q39': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported', 'type': 'yes/no', 'guardrail': True, 'covering': True, 'opened': '2026-08-27'}}\nnew-2 <class 'list'> {'case': 'new-2/clean-1', 'thesis': {'id': 'clean-1', 'description': 'How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed to AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model, and does that contingent exposure become large enough to change its credit risk?', 'outcome': \"The reported amount of NVIDIA's guarantees / credit-support commitments extended to AI cloud customers under the new model.\", 'period': \"NVIDIA's next annual report (Form 10-K), set by section 3 rule for an obligation framework already undertaken; sized at the next annual report.\", 'opens_as': 'binding_obligation', 'settled_by': \"NVIDIA's annual report (Form 10-K) and quarterly filings disclosing guarantees and credit-support commitments, with any confirmed partner-level guarantee amounts.\"}, 'item': {'publication_date': '2026-07-01', 'publisher': 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'title': 'NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog', 'text': 'NVIDIA is partnering with AI clouds to deploy large‑scale, multi‑tenant AI factories, aligning economics through a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.\\nAs AI moves from model development to production inference, compute demand is accelerating and shifting toward continuously operating AI factories that generate tokens at scale. This shift requires access to large‑scale, multi‑tenant accelerated computing that can come online quickly, stay highly utilized and support the economics of token‑scale AI services.\\nEmerging AI companies historically have had limited access to capital-intensive infrastructure, with even long-term commitments insufficient to unlock financing for compute.\\nTo address this, NVIDIA is introducing a new business model that opens up compute access to the fast‑growing AI ecosystem of startups, model builders, enterprises, research organizations and regional AI players.\\nThis new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of NVIDIA platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides NVIDIA with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.\\nFor model builders, inference providers, agent platforms and enterprises scaling AI, it can mean faster access to full-stack accelerated computing without waiting through site selection, power procurement, construction and hardware bring-up.\\nThe initiative is already taking shape, with AI cloud companies building DSX AI factories designed to serve customers and workloads across regions.\\n“This strategic collaboration with NVIDIA marks a pivotal moment in Sharon AI’s mission to deliver sovereign, large-scale AI compute infrastructure,” said James Manning, cofounder and CEO of Sharon AI.\\nFirmus is building a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia. The campus is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n“AI-native companies need access to scalable, energy- and cost-efficient compute infrastructure to compete globally,” said Tim Rosenfield, co-CEO of Firmus Technologies. “Firmus AI cloud is building a NVIDIA DSX-aligned AI factory, which will enable our cloud to help more customers access the comput\nnew-3 <class 'list'> {'case': 'new-3/clean-1', 'thesis': {'id': 'clean-1', 'description': 'How much credit support will NVIDIA have extended to AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing AI-factory model, as disclosed in its periodic filings?', 'outcome': \"The disclosed size of NVIDIA's guarantees, credit support or other contingent backstop obligations to AI cloud partners (or confirmation that none is material).\", 'period': \"NVIDIA's FY2027 annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027), the first annual report after the 2026-07-01 item; the item gives no size or signing date, so the next annual report within 18 months of the item is the check date.\", 'opens_as': 'binding_obligation', 'settled_by': \"NVIDIA's Form 10-K and quarterly Form 10-Q filings, which disclose guarantees, credit support arrangements and other contingent obligations.\"}, 'item': {'publication_date': '2026-07-01', 'publisher': 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'title': 'NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog', 'text': 'NVIDIA is partnering with AI clouds to deploy large‑scale, multi‑tenant AI factories, aligning economics through a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.\\nAs AI moves from model development to production inference, compute demand is accelerating and shifting toward continuously operating AI factories that generate tokens at scale. This shift requires access to large‑scale, multi‑tenant accelerated computing that can come online quickly, stay highly utilized and support the economics of token‑scale AI services.\\nEmerging AI companies historically have had limited access to capital-intensive infrastructure, with even long-term commitments insufficient to unlock financing for compute.\\nTo address this, NVIDIA is introducing a new business model that opens up compute access to the fast‑growing AI ecosystem of startups, model builders, enterprises, research organizations and regional AI players.\\nThis new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of NVIDIA platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides NVIDIA with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.\\nFor model builders, inference providers, agent platforms and enterprises scaling AI, it can mean faster access to full-stack accelerated computing without waiting through site selection, power procurement, construction and hardware bring-up.\\nThe initiative is already taking shape, with AI cloud companies building DSX AI factories designed to serve customers and workloads across regions.\\n“This strategic collaboration with NVIDIA marks a pivotal moment in Sharon AI’s mission to deliver sovereign, large-scale AI compute infrastructure,” said James Manning, cofounder and CEO of Sharon AI.\\nFirmus is building a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia. The campus is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n“AI-native companies need access to scalable, energy- and cost-efficient compute infrastructure to compete globally,” said Tim Rosenfield, co-CEO of Firmus Technologies. “Firmus AI cloud is building a NVIDIA DSX-aligned AI factory, which will ena\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
