6-07-01 v1 20,000,000,000 USD or more []\nQ32 2026-09-10 v53 Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31. []\nnew-3 Counter({'yes/no': 29, 'figure': 12}) ['question_id', 'question', 'due', 'opened', 'opened_from', 'type', 'possible_answers', 'answer', 'answer_index', 'reasons', 'material', 'context', 'source_id']\ncases Counter({'binding_obligation': 22, 'shared_quantity': 15, 'policy_stage': 14, 'product_node': 9})\n[('Q1', 'v1'), ('Q2', 'v2'), ('Q3', 'v3'), ('Q4', 'v5'), ('Q5', 'v7'), ('Q6', 'v8'), ('Q7', 'v10')]\nQ1 2026-07-01 v1 10,000,000,000 USD or more []\nQ13 2026-07-27 v19 By December 31, 2027, NVIDIA has signed a definitive guarantee or credit-support commitment backing the lease or construction debt of OpenAI's planned Ohio campus, and the commitme []\nQ20 2026-08-10 v28 By December 31, 2027, NVIDIA's periodic filings or a formal announcement confirm that definitive agreements for the reported AI data-centre and power-generation financing arrangeme []\nQ38 2026-09-06 v52 The FOMC announces an increase of at least 0.25 percentage points in its federal funds target range at the September 15–16, 2026 meeting, by September 16, 2026. []\nQ39 2026-09-10 v54 Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31. []\nold-1 Counter({'yes/no': 28, 'figure': 19}) ['question_id', 'question', 'due', 'opened', 'opened_from', 'type', 'possible_answers', 'answer', 'answer_index', 'reasons', 'material', 'context', 'source_id']\nQ8 2026-07-06 v8 FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $350 billion and less than $400 billion. []\nQ34 2026-08-26 v34 FY2028 gross margin is at least 71% and below 73%, compared with NVIDIA's stated 72%–73% expectation. []\nold-2 Counter({'yes/no': 26, 'figure': 17}) ['question_id', 'question', 'due', 'opened', 'opened_from', 'type', 'possible_answers', 'answer', 'answer_index', 'reasons', 'material', 'context', 'source_id']\nQ5 2026-07-04 v5 Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion. []\nQ9 2026-07-06 v9 FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion. []\nQ33 2026-08-26 v33 FY2028 gross margin is at least 71% and below 73%. []\nQ40 2026-09-14 v40 NVIDIA does not complete an investment of $10 billion to anchor Anthropic's IPO by 2026-09-20. []\nold-3 Counter({'yes/no': 31, 'figure': 18}) ['question_id', 'question', 'due', 'opened', 'opened_from', 'type', 'possible_answers', 'answer', 'answer_index', 'reasons', 'material', 'context', 'source_id']\nQ6 2026-07-04 v6 Combined spending is at least $700 billion and below $800 billion. []\nQ35 2026-08-19 v35 FY2027 data-center revenue is at least $361 billion but less than $400 billion. []\nQ47 2026-09-14 v47 NVIDIA has not agreed by September 20, 2026, to anchor Anthropic’s IPO with a $10 billion investment. []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/brief-A1.md | sed -n '1,90p'; rg -n 'NVIDIA FY2027 data-center revenue|NVIDIA FY2028 non-GAAP|Anthropic|OpenAI Ohio lease|DOJ enforcement|NVIDIA FY2028 Vera|NVIDIA AI cloud' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json; rg -n 'question\\\": \\\"Will the (DOJ Antitrust|US Department of Justice publish)|combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure|signed and disclosed a definitive guarantee|NVIDIA.s outstanding guarantees|new revenue-sharing AI-factory model is disclosed' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L{3,5}.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/brief-A1.md | sed -n '1,90p'; rg -n 'NVIDIA FY2027 data-center revenue|NVIDIA FY2028 non-GAAP|Anthropic|OpenAI Ohio lease|DOJ enforcement|NVIDIA FY2028 Vera|NVIDIA AI cloud' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json; rg -n 'question\\\": \\\"Will the (DOJ Antitrust|US Department of Justice publish)|combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure|signed and disclosed a definitive guarantee|NVIDIA.s outstanding guarantees|new revenue-sharing AI-factory model is disclosed' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L{3,5}.json\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Blind reader, reading A1: which big questions do these articles raise? (read-only)\n     2\t\n     3\tRepository `/Users/lchingen/hivemind`. You are a senior hedge-fund analyst covering NVIDIA. Read ONLY:\n     4\t`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/packet-A1.json` (40 articles, 2026-09-22 to 09-28, in publication order) and the signed standard\n     5\t`docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html` §3 (the opening reasons and \"问题怎么写\") and §4 (the opening tests: the answer can change a position; a date\n     6\tand public material can settle it; no question already asks the same). Open no other file in that folder or anywhere else: system answers and\n     7\treference answers exist and you must not see them.\n     8\t\n     9\tRead every article in full, first paragraph to last. For each article, list every question worth tracking on its own that it raises: a big\n    10\tmatter (it can change NVIDIA's revenue, profit, cash, credit risk or competitive position, or it is a quantity or decision in the world that\n    11\tmany companies depend on), with an outcome a dated public release, filing or official decision can settle. Small matters, background, a\n    12\trepeat of what an earlier article already raised (list it again only under the same matter key), a stock-price or valuation view, and anything\n    13\tno public material can settle are not questions. Most articles raise none or one; say \"none\" when none qualifies.\n    14\t\n    15\tThen merge: one matter = one underlying bet, whichever articles raise it; another year of a figure is another matter; two questions are one\n    16\tmatter only when the same outcome would settle both and their answers cannot move apart.\n    17\t\n    18\tWrite one JSON object per line:\n    19\t- per question: {\"article\": n, \"matter\": \"<short key>\", \"question\": \"<the question, with its period or check date>\", \"quote\": \"<= 40 words from\n    20\t  the article>\", \"reason\": \"<the §3 reason and why it is big, <= 30 words>\", \"settled_by\": \"<the public material and when>\"}\n    21\t- per article with none: {\"article\": n, \"matter\": null}\n    22\t- finally, per matter: {\"matter\": \"<key>\", \"name\": \"<one line>\", \"articles\": [n, ...]}\n163:   \"name\": \"NVIDIA FY2027 data-center revenue\",\n168:    \"NVIDIA FY2027 data-center revenue\"\n263:   \"name\": \"NVIDIA FY2028 non-GAAP gross margin\",\n269:    \"NVIDIA FY2028 non-GAAP gross margin\",\n360:   \"name\": \"NVIDIA OpenAI Ohio lease guarantee at FY2027 year-end\",\n365:    \"NVIDIA OpenAI Ohio lease guarantee at FY2027 year-end\"\n482:   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign or fund an anchor investment of about $10B in Anthropic's IPO by 2027-03-14 (researcher-set check date), and if so of what size?\",\n483:   \"name\": \"Whether NVIDIA commits an up-to-$10B anchor investment in Anthropic's IPO\",\n490:    \"Whether NVIDIA commits an up-to-$10B anchor investment in Anthropic's IPO\",\n491:    \"NVIDIA Anthropic IPO investment by March 2028\",\n492:    \"NVIDIA Anthropic IPO investment by November 2026\"\n682:   \"name\": \"DOJ enforcement over NVIDIA's Groq arrangement\",\n687:    \"DOJ enforcement over NVIDIA's Groq arrangement\"\n791:   \"name\": \"NVIDIA FY2028 Vera CPU revenue\",\n796:    \"NVIDIA FY2028 Vera CPU revenue\"\n812:   \"name\": \"NVIDIA AI cloud partner guarantee obligations at FY2027 year-end / NVIDIA total third-party guarantees and credit support for cloud/AI partners in the FY2027 10-K (vs up to $108.5B)\",\n817:    \"NVIDIA AI cloud partner guarantee obligations at FY2027 year-end / NVIDIA total third-party guarantees and credit support for cloud/AI partners in the FY2027 10-K (vs up to $108.5B)\"\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L3.json:4:  \"question\": \"What is the total USD amount of NVIDIA's outstanding guarantees and other credit-support commitments extended to AI cloud customers under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model at FY2027 year-end (January 31, 2027), without double-counting, as disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K and supporting commitment disclosures?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L3.json:10339:  \"question\": \"Will the DOJ Antitrust Division publish a formal resolution of its review of Nvidia's Groq licensing transaction by January 31, 2027, as evidenced by a public DOJ statement or court filing?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:4:  \"question\": \"What aggregate amount in USD of guarantees, credit support and other contingent backstop obligations to AI cloud partners under NVIDIA's new revenue-sharing AI-factory model is disclosed as outstanding at FY2027 year-end in its FY2027 Form 10-K, supplemented by its Form 10-Q disclosures, counting an explicit confirmation of no material obligations as zero for this disclosed-material-amount measure?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:353:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:889:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:1814:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:2250:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:2838:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:3485:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:3763:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:4338:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:4644:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:4743:  \"question\": \"By December 31, 2027, will NVIDIA have signed and disclosed a definitive guarantee or credit-support commitment backing the lease or construction debt of OpenAI's planned Ohio AI data center campus, as confirmed by NVIDIA's periodic filings or financing-close disclosures?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:4970:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:5416:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting cohort, as reported in their full-year earnings releases and annual filings?\",\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json:5932:     \"question\": \"What will combined calendar-2026 data-centre capital expenditure be for CoreWeave and Nebius, the two named neoclouds used as the fixed reporting 