{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^'\"' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/round-2/C023-{codex,claude}.json; rg -n '\"'^'\"' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L{1,2}--M04--Q{5,6}--* 2>/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/round-2/C023-claude.json:1:{\"worth\": \"trivia\", \"answer\": \"supported\", \"why\": \"Keeping supported. The material is a forecast basis, not a record of the outcome, but 86% futures pricing (up from 60%), hawkish July dissents and core PCE above 3% clearly favour rung 1 over rungs 2 and 3.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/round-2/C023-codex.json:1:{\"worth\": \"trivia\", \"answer\": \"supported\", \"why\": \"A single rate decision is too indirect to be a material NVIDIA-specific bet. The reported 86% futures probability supports a hike as the most likely forecast, though it does not establish the actual decision.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L2--M04--Q6--codex.json:1:{\"covers\": true, \"why\": \"The question covers data-center capital expenditures by the four hyperscalers in calendar 2026, the main component of their combined capital spending relevant to the matter.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L1--M04--Q5--codex.json:1:{\"covers\": true, \"why\": \"Data-center capital expenditures are a major part of the four hyperscalers’ aggregate spending, and the question captures the main outcome for calendar 2026.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L1--M04--Q5--claude.json:1:{\"covers\": true, \"why\": \"The 'big four AI hyperscalers' are Amazon, Alphabet, Microsoft and Meta. The ~$650B 'data-center capex' figure is their combined total capex, so the same calendar-2026 aggregate settles both. The $100B bands absorb wording differences.\"}\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L2--M04--Q6--claude.json:1:{\"covers\": true, \"why\": \"The 'big four AI hyperscalers' are Amazon, Alphabet, Microsoft and Meta. The article's ~$650B 'data-center capex' figure matches their combined total capex guidance, so one aggregate 2026 number settles both.\"}\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
