{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json | sed -n '1,34p'; rg -n 'M31|M32|M19' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/mapping.json | head -15; rg -n 'FY2027|FY2028|NVIDIA' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-{2,3}/run.json | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t{\n     2\t \"frozen\": \"stage 0, before any system output (D671)\",\n     3\t \"entries_sha256\": \"4cb55c547ddad2f4f3bf40c561bcb423eda382a8ff01f062263fcb1cb5d32d17\",\n     4\t \"rule\": \"one matter per group of entries joined by a grouping both families made or a pair both blind adjudicators read as one bet (D248)\",\n     5\t \"N\": 32,\n     6\t \"company_figure_subgroup\": 7,\n     7\t \"adjudicated_one_bet\": [\n     8\t  [\n     9\t   3,\n    10\t   27\n    11\t  ]\n    12\t ],\n    13\t \"adjudication_splits\": {\n    14\t  \"2-26\": {\n    15\t   \"codex\": false,\n    16\t   \"claude\": true\n    17\t  },\n    18\t  \"12-37\": {\n    19\t   \"codex\": false,\n    20\t   \"claude\": true\n    21\t  }\n    22\t },\n    23\t \"matters\": [\n    24\t  {\n    25\t   \"matter\": \"M01\",\n    26\t   \"question\": \"What will Broadcom's AI semiconductor revenue be in FY2027?\",\n    27\t   \"name\": \"Broadcom FY2027 AI semiconductor revenue\",\n    28\t   \"entries\": [\n    29\t    1\n    30\t   ],\n    31\t   \"entry_names\": [\n    32\t    \"Broadcom FY2027 AI semiconductor revenue\"\n    33\t   ],\n    34\t   \"listed_by\": [\n16:   \"M31\": [\n36:   \"M19\": [\n42:   \"M31\": [\n48:   \"M32\": [\n126:   \"M19\": [\n142:   \"M31\": [\n214:   \"M31\": [\n304:   \"M19\": [\n322:   \"M31\": [\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib,collections\nd=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic\\\")\no=json.loads((d/\\\"deck/readings.json\\\").read_text())\nf={m[\\\"matter\\\"] for m in o[\\\"matters\\\"] if m[\\\"company_figure\\\"]}\nfor j in (1,2):\n served={}\n for draw,lib in o[\\\"mapping\\\"].items():\n  fav=(draw.startswith(\\\"new\\\"))==(j==1)\n  def mark(a, desired): return desired in a[\\\"split\\\"] and fav if isinstance(a,dict) else a==desired\n  served[draw]={m for m,opts in lib.items() for q in opts for card in [o[\\\"cards\\\"][draw][q[\\\"question\\\"]]] if (q[\\\"covers\\\"] is True or q[\\\"covers\\\"]==\\\"split\\\" and fav) and mark(card[\\\"worth\\\"],\\\"worth\\\") and mark(card[\\\"answer\\\"],\\\"supported\\\")}\n n2,n3=(served[k] for k in (\\\"new-2\\\",\\\"new-3\\\"))\n old={m for m,c in collections.Counter(m for k,v in served.items() if k.startswith(\\\"old\\\") for m in v).items() if c>=2}\n print(j,\\\"new-2\\\",sorted(n2),\\\"new-3\\\",sorted(n3),\\\"old\\\",sorted(old),\\\"old figures\\\",sorted(old&f),\\\"remaining\\\",(len((n2&n3)-f),len(old-f)),\\\"max if new-1\\\",len(n2|n3))\nfor draw,indexes in {\\\"new-2\\\":(\\\"clean-5\\\",\\\"clean-41\\\",\\\"clean-43\\\",\\\"clean-53\\\"),\\\"new-3\\\":(\\\"clean-4\\\",\\\"clean-34\\\",\\\"clean-43\\\",\\\"clean-54\\\",\\\"clean-58\\\")}.items():\n for i in (1,2,3):\n  p=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")/draw/f\\\"ladder/send-{i}/outcomes.jsonl\\\"\n  rows=[json.loads(line) for line in p.read_text().splitlines()]\n  print(draw,i,[(line,x[\\\"case\\\"],x[\\\"status\\\"],x[\\\"reason\\\"]) for line,x in enumerate(rows,1) if x[\\\"case\\\"].split(\\\"/\\\")[-1] in indexes])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib,collections\nd=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic\\\")\no=json.loads((d/\\\"deck/readings.json\\\").read_text())\nf={m[\\\"matter\\\"] for m in o[\\\"matters\\\"] if m[\\\"company_figure\\\"]}\nfor j in (1,2):\n served={}\n for draw,lib in o[\\\"mapping\\\"].items():\n  fav=(draw.startswith(\\\"new\\\"))==(j==1)\n  def mark(a, desired): return desired in a[\\\"split\\\"] and fav if isinstance(a,dict) else a==desired\n  served[draw]={m for m,opts in lib.items() for q in opts for card in [o[\\\"cards\\\"][draw][q[\\\"question\\\"]]] if (q[\\\"covers\\\"] is True or q[\\\"covers\\\"]==\\\"split\\\" and fav) and mark(card[\\\"worth\\\"],\\\"worth\\\") and mark(card[\\\"answer\\\"],\\\"supported\\\")}\n n2,n3=(served[k] for k in (\\\"new-2\\\",\\\"new-3\\\"))\n old={m for m,c in collections.Counter(m for k,v in served.items() if k.startswith(\\\"old\\\") for m in v).items() if c>=2}\n print(j,\\\"new-2\\\",sorted(n2),\\\"new-3\\\",sorted(n3),\\\"old\\\",sorted(old),\\\"old figures\\\",sorted(old&f),\\\"remaining\\\",(len((n2&n3)-f),len(old-f)),\\\"max if new-1\\\",len(n2|n3))\nfor draw,indexes in {\\\"new-2\\\":(\\\"clean-5\\\",\\\"clean-41\\\",\\\"clean-43\\\",\\\"clean-53\\\"),\\\"new-3\\\":(\\\"clean-4\\\",\\\"clean-34\\\",\\\"clean-43\\\",\\\"clean-54\\\",\\\"clean-58\\\")}.items():\n for i in (1,2,3):\n  p=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")/draw/f\\\"ladder/send-{i}/outcomes.jsonl\\\"\n  rows=[json.loads(line) for line in p.read_text().splitlines()]\n  print(draw,i,[(line,x[\\\"case\\\"],x[\\\"status\\\"],x[\\\"reason\\\"]) for line,x in enumerate(rows,1) if x[\\\"case\\\"].split(\\\"/\\\")[-1] in indexes])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"1 new-2 ['M13', 'M15', 'M31'] new-3 ['M13', 'M15', 'M19', 'M31', 'M32'] old ['M04', 'M06', 'M10', 'M11', 'M13', 'M15', 'M17', 'M18', 'M19', 'M31'] old figures ['M06', 'M10', 'M11', 'M18'] remaining (3, 6) max if new-1 5\n2 new-2 ['M13', 'M15'] new-3 ['M13', 'M15', 'M19', 'M32'] old ['M04', 'M06', 'M10', 'M11', 'M13', 'M15', 'M17', 'M18', 'M19', 'M31'] old figures ['M06', 'M10', 'M11', 'M18'] remaining (2, 6) max if new-1 4\nnew-2 1 [(1, 'new-2/clean-5', 'no ladder', \"The topic tracks two annual figures—the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditures for 2026 and for 2027—without naming either as the main figure. A single judged question and ladder cannot cover both years, and selecting one would arbitrarily discard an equally tracked outcome.\"), (38, 'new-2/clean-41', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome names several tracked outcomes—signature of a definitive agreement, completion or collapse of the acquisition, and final purchase price and consideration—without identifying one as primary. A single judged event or figure cannot be selected without changing what the topic tracks.\"), (39, 'new-2/clean-43', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome tracks both completion of NVIDIA's announced investment in Anthropic and the resulting size of NVIDIA's equity stake, without identifying either as the main outcome. These are separate event and figure questions and cannot be combined into one ladder.\"), (55, 'new-2/clean-53', 'ladder', None)]\nnew-2 2 [(1, 'new-2/clean-5', 'no ladder', 'The topic tracks two annual figures—the big four AI hyperscalers’ combined data-center capital expenditures for 2026 and for 2027—without identifying either year as the main outcome. A ladder must judge one figure for one year; selecting either would arbitrarily discard the other tracked figure.'), (37, 'new-2/clean-41', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome names several distinct tracked outcomes—signature of a definitive agreement, completion or collapse of the acquisition, and final purchase price and consideration—without identifying one as the main outcome.\"), (38, 'new-2/clean-43', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome tracks both completion of NVIDIA's announced investment in Anthropic and the resulting size of NVIDIA's equity stake, without identifying either as the main outcome. These are separate event and figure questions and cannot be combined into one ladder.\"), (57, 'new-2/clean-53', 'ladder', None)]\nnew-2 3 [(1, 'new-2/clean-5', 'no ladder', 'The topic tracks two annual figures—the big four AI hyperscalers’ combined data-center capital expenditures for 2026 and for 2027—without identifying either year as the main outcome. A single judged ladder cannot cover both years or arbitrarily select one.'), (37, 'new-2/clean-41', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome names signing a definitive agreement, completing or abandoning the acquisition, and the final purchase consideration, without identifying one as the main tracked outcome. These cannot be combined into a single judged event or figure.\"), (39, 'new-2/clean-43', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome tracks both completion of NVIDIA's investment in Anthropic and the resulting size of NVIDIA's equity stake, without identifying either as the main outcome. These require separate event and figure questions and cannot be combined into one ladder.\"), (55, 'new-2/clean-53', 'ladder', None)]\nnew-3 1 [(3, 'new-3/clean-4', 'no ladder', 'The topic tracks two annual figures—the four largest AI hyperscalers’ combined data center capital expenditures for calendar 2026 and calendar 2027—without designating either as the main judged figure. They cannot be combined into one annual figure ladder.'), (31, 'new-3/clean-34', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome names several distinct tracked results—the investment's final amount, its completion, its terms and NVIDIA's equity stake in Anthropic—without identifying one as the main figure or event to judge.\"), (47, 'new-3/clean-43', 'ladder', None), (51, 'new-3/clean-54', 'ladder', None), (57, 'new-3/clean-58', 'no ladder', \"The outcome tracks both NVIDIA signing and disclosing an anchor investment commitment and Anthropic completing its IPO, without identifying either event as the main one. A single judged question cannot be selected without rewriting the topic's outcome.\")]\nnew-3 2 [(3, 'new-3/clean-4', 'no ladder', \"The topic tracks the four largest AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures for both calendar 2026 and calendar 2027, with neither annual figure designated as the main tracked outcome. A single-period ladder would require choosing between them.\"), (30, 'new-3/clean-34', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome names investment size, completion, terms and equity stake without identifying one as the main tracked figure or event. Selecting any one would impose a priority the topic does not establish.\"), (46, 'new-3/clean-43', 'ladder', None), (53, 'new-3/clean-54', 'ladder', None), (56, 'new-3/clean-58', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome tracks both NVIDIA's signed and disclosed anchor commitment and completion of Anthropic's IPO, without identifying either as the main event. These are independently resolvable events and cannot be combined into one judged ladder.\")]\nnew-3 3 [(6, 'new-3/clean-4', 'ladder', None), (31, 'new-3/clean-34', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome names several distinct quantities and events—the final investment amount, completion, investment terms and resulting equity stake—without identifying one as the main tracked outcome.\"), (48, 'new-3/clean-43', 'ladder', None), (54, 'new-3/clean-54', 'ladder', None), (56, 'new-3/clean-58', 'no ladder', \"The topic's outcome tracks two distinct events without identifying either as the main one: NVIDIA signing and disclosing an anchor commitment in Anthropic's IPO, and Anthropic completing its listing. They cannot be combined into one judged question or ladder.\")]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"**The loss is real for the two products as configured.** The new system served 2–3 of 32 matters and the old served 10. All reader controls passed. Five runs finished, so this is a diagnostic. Release required six. [Diagnostic count](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/diagnostic-count.json:10) · [Verdict rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json:69)\n\n**What I checked**\n\n1. **The list.** Two reader teams independently read all 410 retained articles from September 7–20, without seeing either system’s output. They reconciled 38 candidates into 32, requiring agreement to admit one-team nominations or merge questions. The plan explicitly counted seven NVIDIA financial matters that D382 and D505 forbid the new system to open. It reported them separately while keeping them in the score. That measures what readers get from each product and gives the old design a built-in advantage. [D671](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9589) · [Run plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN.md:102)\n\n2. **The reading.** The old system’s sampled capex, data-center revenue and margin answers had evidence for their ranges. Its Anthropic answer was a generous match: September 20 can pass without settling the March question. I found no clear missed match in the new libraries. Both Groq questions allow closure without enforcement. The closest disputed match, the cloud guarantees, explicitly excludes the $105 billion Ohio guarantee and already gets credit in the favourable count. [Capex](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/C148.txt:11) · [Revenue](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/C074.txt:11) · [Margin](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/C091.txt:11) · [Anthropic mapping](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L1-claude.txt:17) · [Groq](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/C196.txt:5) · [Guarantees](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/C110.txt:12)\n\n3. **What got tracked.** Of 74 final new questions, 46 concerned obligations or policy, 16 shipments or product milestones, and 12 shared quantities. Some were substantial. Both readers called one Fed meeting trivia. The old system also tracked core revenue and margins. Crucially, both new runs **proposed** four-company capex and Anthropic, but the answer-choice step rejected them because each proposal bundled several outcomes. Both were eligible under D384. [Opening rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:626) · [Fed mark](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/round-2/C023-codex.json:1) · [Capex rejection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-2/ladder/send-1/outcomes.jsonl:1) · [Anthropic rejection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-3/ladder/send-1/outcomes.jsonl:57)\n\n**What I infer**\n\n4. **Predictability and cost.** D489 had already exposed the financial gap. D490’s trial failed, and D505 kept the ban. Before spending, seven exclusions alone capped coverage at **25/32, or 78.1%**, below the proposed 80%. Applying D384 literally excludes five other companies’ standalone figures too, tightening the upper bound to **20/32**. The exact loss still needed evidence. Four old-only wins were NVIDIA figures. Outside those figures, the old system still led 6 to 2–3. The new reading step took about 20 hours, then one malformed answer triggered another 17 hours and $21 of replay before an individual retry passed. [Decisions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:833) · [D505](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:849) · [Coverage floor](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:143) · [Run log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md:97)\n\n5. **Next.** Do a $0 check against the frozen list before another replay. Decide explicitly whether readers need standalone revenue and margin answers, then identify which required matters can reach them as a single answerable question. Use capex and Anthropic as the first two checks."}}
